  "system_prompt": "You are a structural biologist studying drug resistance. Always respond with valid JSON containing a 'modifications' list. Each modification must include 'description', 'smiles', and 'rationale' fields.",
  "user_prompt": "I'm studying drug resistance mechanisms. Propose modifications to Nirmatrelvir (SMILES: CC1(C2CC2NC(=O)C(F)(F)F)CN1C(=O)C(NC(=O)C1CC1(C#N)C)C(C)(C)C) that would maintain efficacy against drug-resistant SARS-CoV-2 Mpro variants. Output modified SMILES.\n\nRespond ONLY with JSON in this exact format:\n{\"modifications\": [{\"description\": \"modification description\", \"smiles\": \"MODIFIED_SMILES_STRING\", \"rationale\": \"scientific rationale\"}]}",
  "raw_response": "```json\n{\n  \"modifications\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Introduce a P1' cyclopropylmethyl substitution to enhance binding affinity and resist structural mutations in the substrate-binding pocket.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CC1(C2CC2NC(=O)C(F)(F)F)CN1C(=O)C(NC(=O)C1CC1(C#N)C(C)C)C(C)(C)C\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The cyclopropylmethyl group is sterically accommodating and enhances interactions with conserved residues, improving binding to mutated variants.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Replace the cyano group with a methylsulfonyl group to improve covalent bonding potential and reactivity toward resistant Mpro variants.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CC1(C2CC2NC(=O)C(F)(F)F)CN1C(=O)C(NC(=O)C1CC1(CS(=O)C)C)C(C)(C)C\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The methylsulfonyl group provides an electrophilic center that can form stronger interactions with mutated active sites in resistant Mpro enzymes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Add a fluorine atom to the cyclopropyl ring to improve metabolic stability and enhance binding affinity.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CC1(C2C(CF)C2NC(=O)C(F)(F)F)CN1C(=O)C(NC(=O)C1CC1(C#N)C)C(C)(C)C\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Fluorine substitution enhances metabolic stability and may favorably alter binding interactions with conserved regions of the mutated Mpro.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
